{title: Meager Rations}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 22:26–27; 2 Chronicles 18:25–26; 1 Kings 22:34–37}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The king gave his command to the governor
Hand the prophet over [Gm]to the city walls
With Joash the son of the [Bb]crown
Keep the [C]man behind the [Dm]bars
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Say thus says the king to the prisoner
Put this man [Gm]in prison for his words
Give him only [Bb]meager rations of bread
And [C]water until I return [Dm]safely
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The word of the Lord cannot be bound
Though the governor keeps [Bb]the door [C]locked [F]tight
No prison can [Gm]hold the truth of [Bb]God
The prophecy [C]stands before the [Dm]king
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Someone drew his bow at random aim
Struck the [Bb]king between the sec[C]tions of ar[Dm]mor
[Gm]Turn around and get me out of the [Bb]fight
For I am [C]wounded and dying [Dm]now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
The battle grew fierce that very day
The king was [Bb]propped up in his [C]chariot
Facing the A[Bb]rameans in the dust
That [C]evening he died in the [Dm]blood
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]A cry spread through the army [C]at sunset
Ev[Am]ery man to his own city and [Dm]land
The [Bb]king died and was brought to [C]Samaria
And they [Am]buried him in the [Dm]ground
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Bb]meager rations [C]could not [Dm]save him
[Bb]The word of [C]the Lord came [Dm]true
{end_of_verse}
